$$\\theta ^{7}\(1-\\theta \)^{3}$$
](A442674_1_En_9_Chapter_IEq47.gif) which is graphed in Fig. 9.2. The figure also shows ![
$$\\theta ^{3}\(1-\\theta \)^{7}$$
](A442674_1_En_9_Chapter_IEq48.gif) which is proportional to the posterior for 3 heads and 7 tails. In each case, the evidence does not rule out the possibility that θ = 0. 5, but tends to discourage the conclusion. Maximum likelihood would give θ = 0

